say which files an application actually reads, and how many bytes

iA Writer opens a document and shows nothing, and the file coordinator says the read RAN, so the
open question in #194 was what happens to the bytes afterwards. Nothing in the log could say
whether the bytes ever arrived.

_NSReadBytesFromFile is the funnel under every Foundation file read: NSData initWithContentsOfFile,
NSString initWithContentsOfFile:encoding:, and the URL forms of both. CIDER_TRACE_READ prints its
path, its byte count and whether it succeeded. -[NSString initWithData:encoding:] prints the byte
count, the encoding and the resulting length, because an application that reads bytes ITSELF and
decodes them there never touches the URL methods at all, and iA Writer is one: initWithData:encoding:
is the only string from bytes selector its binary and its Kit framework carry, which llvm-nm and
strings agree on.

WHAT IT SAID IMMEDIATELY, and it removes file reading from #194 with a POSITIVE measurement rather
than an absence:

  CIDER_READ bytes path=/Users/root/Documents/Cider.md length=40 ok

All forty bytes of the document reach the application through Foundation. And in the same run
-[NSString initWithData:encoding:] was called ZERO times, so whatever iA Writer does with those
bytes, it does not decode them through NSString. A Swift application decoding with
String(decoding:as:) would look exactly like that, and that is pure Swift with no Foundation call.

Bounded at 200 lines each and gated, and the gate is cached rather than a getenv per call because
this sits under every read an application makes.
--- a/src/_NSFileIO.m
+++ b/src/_NSFileIO.m
@@ -21,6 +21,31 @@
 #import <sys/stat.h>
 #import "NSErrorInternal.h"
 
+/* EVERY FILE READ FOUNDATION MAKES comes through here, so this is the one place that can say
+ * whether an application read a file at all and how many bytes it got. iA Writer opens a document
+ * and shows nothing, and the coordinated read RUNS, so the question is what happens to the bytes
+ * afterwards (#194). Bounded and off unless asked for. */
+static void _CiderTraceRead(NSString *path, NSUInteger length, BOOL ok)
+{
+    static int cached = -1;
+    static int printed;
+
+    if (cached < 0)
+    {
+        const char *value = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_READ");
+
+        cached = (value != NULL && value[0] != '\0') ? 1 : 0;
+    }
+    if (cached == 0 || printed >= 200)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    printed++;
+    fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_READ bytes path=%s length=%lu %s\n", [path UTF8String] ?: "(nil)",
+            (unsigned long)length, ok ? "ok" : "FAILED");
+    fflush(stderr);
+}
+
 void *_NSReadBytesFromFile(NSString *path, NSDataReadingOptions readOptionsMask, NSUInteger *length, BOOL *vm, NSError **err)
 {
     *length = 0;
@@ -28,6 +53,7 @@
     int fd = open([path UTF8String], O_RDONLY);
     if (fd < 0)
     {
+        _CiderTraceRead(path, 0, NO);
         if (err != NULL)
         {
             *err = [NSError errorWithDomain:NSPOSIXErrorDomain code:errno userInfo:@{NSLocalizedDescriptionKey: [NSString stringWithUTF8String:strerror(errno)]}];
@@ -147,6 +173,7 @@
 
     close(fd);
 
+    _CiderTraceRead(path, *length, YES);
     return bytes;
 }
 
